// Proofs for the identities barista.hana states, in the strategy language of
// docs/proving.md. An identity with no entry here is proved by `diagram`
// alone — this file holds exactly the claims that need direction.

// The contract claim, and the corpus's biggest goal: 351 boxes against 2
// once `inline` has opened it. It closes as a decision tree of three
// hypotheses, written as structured `cases` (docs/proving.md) and
// compiled to one checked derivation per side.
//
// The two `is_symbol` splits are written as *arms* and the state split is
// not, and that is the whole of what the shape says: an unaddressed
// `cases` takes the first wire it is offered, and both tag tests are
// `is_symbol` on one `untuple`'s answers, so the second split has to be
// written inside the first's true arm — where the first wire is a literal
// and no longer on offer — or it picks the same one twice and stands
// still.
//
// One state decides everything: `emit` dispatches on `equal(x.2,
// state::thirsty)`, and the driver has already identified that test with
// the precondition disjunction's own — one wire, two readers — so the
// split is addressed by its literal, not left to whichever `equal` sits
// outermost (that would be the tuple-shape guard, forever). In the false
// case `emit` answers a false flag and the postcondition holds vacuously,
// whatever the precondition said — the whole disjunction is moot. In the
// true case `emit` builds the PushBack event outright; the tuple rows
// (`tuple-cancel`, `as-tuple-built`, `equal-refl`) take the
// postcondition's shape guards apart until its symbol checks are the very
// boxes the precondition tested, and the two `is_symbol` splits decide
// them — each false case discharged by `and-literal`, each true case
// folding the conjunction shut.
proof barista::customer_impl::emit_does_pre_and_post_is_constant =
    inline both(decide)
    cases(equal(state::thirsty)) both(decide)
    cases(is_symbol) (
        true: both(decide) cases(is_symbol) (
            true: both(decide),
            false: both(decide)),
        false: both(decide))
    diagram;
